    <hint format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The integral involves an exponential function, \(e^x\), which grows rapidly for \(x\gt 0\)</p>
<p>To evaluate the improper integral, rewrite it as a limit</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_limit@}}^{{@upper_limit@}}{@func@}\,dx=\lim_{b \to \infty } \int_{{@lower_limit@}}^{b}{@func@}\,dx \)</p>
<p>For an improper integral to converge, the function being integrated must decrease rapidly enough to approach zero as \(x\to \infty \)</p>]]></text>
